3. HOW OCEANBRIDGE SETTLES
   (IMPORTANT)

  All fees, credits, and
  liquidation balances flow
  through the SAME merchant
  account that generates your
  weekly disbursements:

    - Negative balances net
      against the next weekly
      disbursement (if a
      disbursement is too
      small, the balance
      carries forward)
    - We never invoice by
      email, never request
      wire transfers, and
      have no "regional
      collections" entity
      that bills customers

  OceanBridge will NEVER:
  - Ask you to wire a
    settlement to any named
    account, including a
    subsidiary-style
    beneficiary such as
    "OBF Regional Collections
    Sp. z o.o." (3PL fraud
    typically uses an EU
    subsidiary name plus an
    IBAN in a different
    country)
  - Use lookalike domains
    such as "oceanbridge-3pl"
    or "ob-returns-settle"
  - Threaten automatic
    returns suspension plus
    a reactivation fee in
    the same message that
    first presents a
    balance (account
    actions follow the
    contract's cure periods,
    not an email deadline)

